    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0329" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/3086</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-16T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>520. [For Grew<anchor n="1" xml:id="d243-f1"/>]:</p>
                <p>Your 1817, 7th, and 1836, 14th. If the Austro-Hungarian Government will eliminate
                    the restriction of four weeks for the departure of American citizens mentioned
                    in paragraph 1 and will add to paragraph 3 the words “or a menace to the
                    national safety,” this Government will accept the proposed reciprocal
                    arrangement. It will be observed that paragraph 2 is unnecessary and should be
                    eliminated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="1" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p> J. C. Grew, Chargé in Austria-Hungary from Apr. 7 to 14, departed on the latter
                    date for Berne, Switzerland, accompanied by the entire Embassy staff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
